   "file": "TauCeti/FieldTheory/RealClosure/OddExtension.lean",
   "fix": "Keep the AdjoinRoot lemmas as the descent step and add the general form: `theorem extensionCone.neg_one_notMem_of_odd_finrank [Field L] [Algebra K L] [FiniteDimensional K L] (h : Odd (Module.finrank K L)) : -1 \u2209 extensionCone (algebraMap K L)` plus the corresponding `exists_linearOrder` corollary. Proof: `IsStrictOrderedRing.toCharZero` gives separability, `Field.exists_primitive_element` gives \u03b1 with K\u27ee\u03b1\u27ef = \u22a4, `IntermediateField.adjoin.finrank` and `finrank_top'` give `Odd (minpoly K \u03b1).natDegree`, then transport a certificate along `(IntermediateField.adjoinRootEquivAdjoin K (IsIntegral ..)).symm` composed with the top equiv using an `extensionCone.map_mem` lemma for K-algebra homs (same induction as `extensionCone.aeval_mem`), and apply `neg_one_notMem_adjoinRoot`.",
   "issue": "`AdjoinRoot.exists_linearOrder` (and `extensionCone.neg_one_notMem_adjoinRoot`) are the only public forms of the odd-degree extension result; the roadmap bullet (README.md:151) states it for any finite field extension L/K of odd degree, and a user with `[FiniteDimensional K L]` and `Odd (finrank K L)` cannot apply the AdjoinRoot form without redoing the primitive-element reduction.",
